# b needs itself, so it derives no finite input, and so do b+ and top,
# which use it. Only the cause is reported, at b's alternative: not the
# helper b+, not top, and never the internal accept rule.
# error: unproductive_cascade.grammar:17:5: error: rule b derives no finite input
# absent: rule top
# absent: rule b+
# absent: $accept
@lexer
tokens
    x
    eof
    err
'x' → x
.   → err
@parser
top! = X b+
b = X b
